  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ROAP/AFG02/23/Socio-economic recovery of earthquake affected populations through cash for work (CfW) support.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In June 2022, Afghanistan was hit by an earthquake leaving over 600 people dead and over 500,000 in need of humanitarian assistance. Many humanitarian actors responded immediately by providing lifesaving assistance to the affected populations. However, assessments indicate that more assistance is still needed especially to support disaster risk reduction (DRR) activities. UN-Habitat with support from the State of Kuwait, will implement a socio-economic recovery project by supporting livelihoods while strengthening community resilience through construction of DRR infrastructure. This proposed action deploys a community-based approach to strengthen ownership and community resilience to disasters.</narrative>
  </description>
